.TH LIBMPQ__BLOCK_COMPRESSION 3 2026-09-11 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__block_compression \- query the effective compression of one block
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__block_compression("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s *" "archive",
.BI "        uint32_t       " "file_number",
.BI "        uint32_t       " "block_number",
.BI "        uint32_t      *" "compression"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Report the actual stored compression method of a logical block. Zero means
raw storage, including a compressed file's per-sector raw fallback. Legacy
IMPLODE blocks return LIBMPQ_COMPRESSION_PKZIP (0x08) when stored imploded.
COMPRESS blocks return their serialized method byte, including combinations
such as SPARSE with zlib (0x22).
.PP
Method 0x12 denotes the legacy bzip2/zlib chain in MPQ v1 and LZMA in MPQ v2.
It is not the writer-only LIBMPQ_COMPRESSION_LZMA selector. The query does not
apply writer compatibility policies or validate the compressed stream.
.PP
The reader manages sector offsets internally and decrypts only the packed
prefix needed to inspect the method. No block decompression or checksum
verification occurs. Single-unit files, encrypted blocks, final partial
sectors and sector checksum tables use the normal reader interpretation;
checksum-table bytes are never considered data blocks.
.PP
Encrypted method prefixes require a known or recoverable reader key. In
particular, encrypted single-unit COMPRESS files have no sector offset table
for key recovery and can return LIBMPQ_ERROR_DECRYPT, as ordinary reads do.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns LIBMPQ_SUCCESS and stores the method in *compression on success.
A non-NULL output is initialized to zero before validation and remains zero
on failure. LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST indicates NULL required arguments or an invalid
file/block index. LIBMPQ_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED indicates a writer archive.
Malformed offsets, out-of-range payloads, I/O, decryption and allocation
failures retain the existing reader's negative error codes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__file_flags (3),
.BR libmpq__block_size_packed (3),
.BR libmpq__block_size_unpacked (3),
.BR libmpq__block_read (3),
.BR libmpq__block_verify (3)
